# lgamma.cyr — lnΓ within 2 ulp (T1, M2 part b3; port plan D3 = C, §3.4; ADR 009: ≤ 2 ulp for x > 0, and ≤ 2 ulp
# of max(|lnΓ|, 1) for x < 0).
#
# Probe P9's prototype (§5 step 9d-1), moved here unchanged but for names. It is fdlibm's e_lgamma_r layout:
# polynomials centred on the roots at 1 and 2 and on the minimum at 1.4616, the rational form on [2, 3) with the
# product (y + 2)(y + 3)… up to 8, and the asymptotic series from 8. Three changes keep a rounding from costing an
# ulp:
# - every logarithm is kimiya's double-double ln core (src/crmath.cyr, relative error near 2^-80), not a rounded ln;
# - the product on [3, 8), and (x − ½)(ln x − 1) for x ≥ 8 at every magnitude up to lnΓ's overflow, are carried as
#   double-doubles (fdlibm drops the −½ past 2^58);
# - for x < 0, sin(πx) is reduced exactly, r = |x| − round(|x|), and the reflection subtracts in double-double.
# The result is rounded once. P9 measured it within 1.31 ulp for x > 0 and 1.40 ulp of max(|lnΓ|, 1) for x < 0 on
# 1,675,000 MPFR rows, where 1.3.0's Lanczos form is off by up to 4.3×10¹³ ulp beside the roots.
#
# Unlike 1.3.0: lnΓ(x) = −ln x for 0 < x < 2^-70 (1.3.0 returned +∞ below about 3.2e-301); the negative integers are
# poles, +∞ (1.3.0 returned a finite value, as sin(π·n) rounds away from 0); and lnΓ(±∞) = +∞ (1.3.0: NaN at +∞).
# The coefficients are src/lgamma_data.cyr's, which scripts/vendor_lgamma.py generates from the libm crate's
# transcription of e_lgamma_r.c and checks, with this file's inline hex words (`--check`).
#
# UPSTREAM(L8): ganita:docs/development/issues/2026-11-15-special-functions-scope-request.md
#   replace with ganita's lgamma if it takes the special functions on, at ADR 009's bound; parity: every ln_gamma row
#
